Third-party code in kda-indexer
===============================

All dependencies of the default build are under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, zlib, ISC,
BSL-1.0, Unicode-3.0 or CDLA-Permissive-2.0 terms (or dual-licensed with one of
them). The notices below cover code that is vendored or statically linked with
terms that ask for attribution beyond the crate metadata.

ptr_hash 2.1.3 (vendor/ptr_hash)
  Copyright (c) Ragnar Groot Koerkamp. MIT licence, see vendor/ptr_hash/LICENSE-MIT.
  Source: https://github.com/RagnarGrootKoerkamp/ptrhash
  Modified: the `colored` dependency (MPL-2.0) and its one use (bold log output in
  src/util.rs) are removed; examples and dev-dependencies are dropped. Added
  `PtrHash::from_saved_parts`, `saved_parts` and `saved_sizes` (persisting and
  validating an index). The pilot search in src/build.rs uses a fixed per-part
  seed, so builds are reproducible.

reth storage crates (reth-libmdbx, reth-mdbx-sys, reth-nippy-jar, reth-fs-util)
  Copyright (c) the reth contributors. reth is MIT OR Apache-2.0; reth-libmdbx and
  reth-mdbx-sys are Apache-2.0. Source: https://github.com/paradigmxyz/reth
  (release v2.10.1, commit 58ebce14ae63dab040beae301e1578cd0dc55e8a).

libmdbx (bundled by reth-mdbx-sys, statically linked)
  Copyright 2015-2026 Leonid Yuriev <leo@yuriev.ru>. Apache-2.0.
  libmdbx ships a NOTICE file with its source; it is reproduced in packages that
  contain the binary (packaging/debian/libmdbx-NOTICE; installed as
  /usr/share/doc/kda-indexer/NOTICE.libmdbx). Source: https://libmdbx.dqdkfa.ru

chainweb-data (crates/kdx-api/data/{miner_rewards.csv,token_payments.csv}, src/supply.rs)
  The two CSV files are copied from kda-community/chainweb-data (haskell-src/data), and
  src/supply.rs reproduces the circulating-supply formula of its Chainweb.Coins module.
  The comparison harness (crates/kdx-compare/src/rewards.rs) embeds miner_rewards.csv.
  BSD-3-Clause. The licence text of that repository follows.

